# nr-tui-pickers-model: what the application (nr-tui-app-run) and the lead apply

No Cargo, workspace, protocol or SERVICE_PENDING change: mixdog-tui already depends on mixdog-tui-widgets, mixdog-view-model,
mixdog-js and mixdog-tui-style, and the pickers call only store methods the store already serves. Nothing to remove from
SERVICE_PENDING in compose_flip.rs.

## Implement `mixdog_tui::pickers::common::PickerHost` for the application context (src/app.rs, task nr-tui-app-run)

One impl beside the SlashHost impl (same struct). The picker functions run against `&mut dyn PickerHost`; every method has the
Node meaning noted on it. What the host must provide:

- `paint_picker(claim, panel)`: the guarded write of `PanelSurface::set_picker` (true claim check: `epoch().is_current(claim.epoch)`),
  answering `surface_claim(SurfaceKind::Picker)` re-armed after the write; `None` when refused. `PickerPanel` implements
  `PanelValue` (identity = kind, else title) and `IndexModePanel`, so it is the `P` of `PanelSurface<PickerPanel, C, U>`.
- `close_surface(claim)`: `set_picker(None)` and a supersede of the epoch (a closed claim is released for good: a late result of
  that picker must not repaint it).
- `clear_context_panel(claim)`: `PanelClaim::context(None)` semantics (guarded, clears the context panel, supersedes, answers the
  re-armed claim).
- `model_caches()`: one `ModelCatalogCaches` in the application state. `clear_model_caches(scope)` of SlashHost is
  `model_caches().clear(scope)`; when it answers true the onboarding state's own provider models are cleared too
  (`onboardingRef.current.providerModels = []`).
- `schedule_catalog_refresh(job)`: run `mixdog_tui::pickers::model::catalog::run_catalog_refresh(host, job)` off the open that asked
  (a task/thread that owns the store connection); it only fills the cache for the NEXT open.
- `open_provider_setup(request)`: open the Providers picker (title, continue label and description) and call
  `request.on_continue` where the Node `onContinue` was called.
- `route_state()`: provider, model, effort, fast, modelParameters, contextPercent, effortOptions, busy of the live state.
- the picker view: build `PickerPanel::props(columns)` for the widget; the view reports the highlighted row to
  `handler.on_highlight` when `handler.wants_highlight()` (including once for the initial selection, as the Node picker did on
  mount), and Enter, Left, Right, Tab, other keys, Esc and the confirm bar to the handler's `on_select`, `on_left`, `on_right`,
  `on_tab`, `on_key`, `on_cancel`, `on_confirm(button.value)`.

## Opener names (SlashHost::open / Opener) to the picker functions

    Opener::Model        -> pickers::model::open_model_picker(host, ModelPickerOptions::default())   (options.refresh_models for `/model refresh`)
    Opener::WebSearch    -> pickers::model::web_search::open_web_search_picker
    Opener::Agents       -> pickers::model::agents::open_agents_picker   (AgentsOptions.refresh_models for `/agents refresh`)
    Opener::Workflow     -> pickers::model::workflow::open_workflow_picker
    Opener::OutputStyle  -> pickers::model::output_style::open_output_style_picker
    Opener::Theme        -> pickers::model::theme::open_theme_picker
    Opener::Effort       -> pickers::model::theme::open_effort_picker

The onboarding steps call open_theme_picker / open_output_style_picker with `Onboarding { on_advance, on_back, on_cancel }`.

## Boot warm-up

`PREFETCH_DELAY_MS` (1500) after start the application calls `pickers::model::catalog::prefetch_catalogs(host)` once from a task
(cancelled when the application exits).

## Store bindings the pickers call

`store_call` names and arguments are exactly the Node store methods: listProviderModels({quick}|{force}), listWebSearchModels,
getProviderSetup, setRoute(routeInput), getWebSearchRoute, setWebSearchRoute, listAgents, setAgentRoute(id, route | {disabled:true}),
listWorkflows, setWorkflow(id), listOutputStyles, setOutputStyle(id), listThemes, getTheme, setTheme(id, {persist}), setEffort(value).
A method the store does not have answers `Ok(Null)`. The theme calls stay local to the process: `listThemes`, `getTheme` and `setTheme`
are bound to `mixdog_tui_style::theme::{list_themes, get_theme_setting, set_theme}` (the live preview, applied first) and `setTheme`
with `persist: true` also writes `ui.theme` through the core's `config/setTheme`.

## Route writes (nr-tui-sv-store)

`pickers::model::route_write` is the serialized optimistic `setRoute` of routes-write.mjs as a pure state machine
(`optimistic_route_patch`, `RouteRequest::from_options`, `complete_session_only_request`, `RouteWrites::{begin, settle, finish}`).
The store's `setRoute` handler (lead route, agent child routes with `sessionOnly`) runs its writes one after another in the order
`begin` hands out tokens, publishes `WriteBegin::preview` at once, and applies `Settlement` after each write: only the write holding
the newest token publishes the final route or rolls the preview back, so a late catalog response never rolls back a newer route.
